{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.KnotRegistry","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:QOU.KnotTheory","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":43,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.figureEight_crossing_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.figureEight_crossing_count","kind":"theorem","line":310,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L310-L313","doc":"The figure-eight knot has 4 crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.trefoil_crossing_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.trefoil_crossing_count","kind":"theorem","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L305-L308","doc":"The trefoil has 3 crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.unknot_crossing_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.unknot_crossing_count","kind":"theorem","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L300-L303","doc":"The unknot has 0 crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.unknot_volume_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.unknot_volume_zero","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L293-L296","doc":"The unknot has zero hyperbolic volume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.trefoil_volume_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.trefoil_volume_zero","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L288-L291","doc":"The trefoil (torus knot) has zero hyperbolic volume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.figureEight_volume_consistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.figureEight_volume_consistent","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L281-L286","doc":"The figure-eight volume extracted from the registry matches the\nconstant used in `MassDerivation`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.KnotEntry.volumeValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.KnotEntry.volumeValue","kind":"def","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L277-L279","doc":"Extract the hyperbolic volume value from a registry entry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.lookupByIdentity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.lookupByIdentity","kind":"def","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L271-L273","doc":"Look up a knot entry by its QOU physical identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.lookup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.lookup","kind":"def","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L267-L269","doc":"Look up a knot entry by its Alexander-Briggs index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.registry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.registry","kind":"def","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L259-L263","doc":"The complete knot registry: all knots with settled types in the QOU\nformalization.  Ordered by Alexander-Briggs crossing number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.borromeanRingsEntry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.borromeanRingsEntry","kind":"def","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L211-L255","doc":"**Borromean Rings (6₂³)** — three mutually linked rings, no two\nof which are linked pairwise.\nQOU identity: **Nucleon**.  The Borromean topology encodes the\ncolor-exchange entanglement of three quark tubes (uud or udd).\n\nMathematical value (exact, transcendental): `8 · G` where\n`G` = Catalan's constant (OEIS A006752).  The `volume.value`\nfield below is the 50-dps decimal *approximation* to that exact\nvalue — the EXACT symbol lives in `QOU.Archimedean.vol_B3`\n(defined as `8 · catalan_G`).\n\nKnot Atlas: <http://katlas.org/wiki/L6a4>\nHyperbolic volume (catalog literal): 50 dps,\n`7.32772475341775212043682811945907288619319499425336`\n`± 1×10⁻⁵⁰`.  Bumped 2026-06-07 from the previous 15-dps\nliteral `7.32772475341775 ± 1×10⁻¹⁴` to match the project's\nstandard working serialization precision (50 dps per\n`computations/_precision.py`).\nSource: **mpmath `mp.catalan` at `mp.dps = 50`, evaluated as\n`8 * mp.catalan`** — a closed-form-derived decimal (computed\nfrom the exact identity `Vol(L6a4) = 8·G`), NOT a SnapPy\nnumerical measurement. The numerical value agrees with SnapPy's\n`M = SnapPy.Manifold(\"L6a4\"); M.volume()` to 15+ digits (and\nwith the proof of Adams (1985) that the two are equal), but\nthe literal stored here is computed from the closed form so\nits precision is bounded by `mp.dps`, not by SnapPy's `f64`\nconvergence floor. (Copilot review #1978: previous docstring\nconflated the two provenances.)\nComponents: 3\n\nNote: this `value` field is a data-catalog decimal kept for\ndownstream consumers that want a literal rather than the\nsymbolic form. The categorical `QOU.Archimedean.vol_B3` is\nthe EXACT transcendental (`8 · catalan_G`) — use it in\nproofs and as the canonical Borromean volume reference. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.hopfLinkEntry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.hopfLinkEntry","kind":"def","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L193-L209","doc":"**Hopf Link (L2a1)** — the simplest non-trivial link (2 components).\nQOU identity: **Strong Force**.  The Hopf link represents the\ninternal binding energy between quarks; invisible to the ℂP¹ base.\n\nKnot Atlas: <http://katlas.org/wiki/Hopf_Link>\nHyperbolic volume: 0  (torus link — non-hyperbolic)\nComponents: 2 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.barePhoton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.barePhoton","kind":"def","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L189-L191","doc":"The bare (free) photon: all colour weights vanish, leaving the\nidentity term `𝟙` alone — the limit recorded by `photonEntry`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.photonSupportWords_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.photonSupportWords_length","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L183-L187","doc":"The photon is a **four-term** element: its support has four basis\nwords, distinguishing it from the single-component unknot `0₁`\n(the neutrino). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.photonSupportWords","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.photonSupportWords","kind":"def","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L179-L181","doc":"The four basis words carrying the photon, as `σ`-index sequences:\n`𝟙 = []`, `σ₀ = [0]`, `σ₁ = [1]`, `σ₀σ₁ = [0,1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.PhotonHeckeElement.phi01","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.PhotonHeckeElement.phi01","kind":"def","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L177-L177","doc":"Colour weight of `σ₀σ₁ = L₊`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.PhotonHeckeElement.phi1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.PhotonHeckeElement.phi1","kind":"def","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L175-L175","doc":"Colour weight of `σ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.PhotonHeckeElement.phi0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.PhotonHeckeElement.phi0","kind":"def","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L173-L173","doc":"Colour weight of `σ₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.PhotonHeckeElement.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.PhotonHeckeElement.mk","kind":"ctor","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L171-L171","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.PhotonHeckeElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.PhotonHeckeElement","kind":"structure","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L168-L177","doc":"The photon as a four-term element of the Hecke algebra `H₃(q)`:\n`γ = 𝟙 + φ₀·σ₀ + φ₁·σ₁ + φ₀₁·σ₀σ₁`.  The colour weights are formal,\nso this is stated over a generic commutative ring (no `q₀`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.photonEntry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.photonEntry","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L125-L155","doc":"**Empty Knot (photon background)** — the identity braid\n$\\mathbf{1}$ with zero crossings.\nQOU identity: **Photon**.  Represents the background flux on the\nexceptional divisor.  The closure of the identity braid is a\ndisjoint union of unknots; the entry is distinguished from the\nsingle-component unknot ($0_1$, the neutrino) by carrying no\nstrand at all in its bare presentation.  Both have Jones\npolynomial $1$, so transfer-matrix arithmetic coincides, but the\nphysical roles differ: photon (empty knot, $\\varnothing$) vs.\nneutrino (unknot, $0_1$).  This entry records only the **bare**\nphoton; the genuine photon is the four-term Hecke element\n`PhotonHeckeElement` defined below.\n\nKnot Atlas (closest entry, single-strand limit):\n<http://katlas.org/wiki/0_1> ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.figureEightEntry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.figureEightEntry","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L108-L123","doc":"**Figure-Eight Knot (4₁)** — the simplest hyperbolic knot.\nQOU identity: **Higgs field (mass mechanism)**.  Its hyperbolic volume\nVol(4₁) ≈ 2.02988321281931 is the numerator in the mass-ratio derivation\n`m_μ/m_e = Vol(4₁) / ℏ_q²`.  The figure-eight is amphichiral\n(4₁ = 4₁⁻¹), so the Higgs field is its own antiparticle.\nExact: 3 · Cl₂(π/3) (OEIS A091518).\n\nKnot Atlas: <http://katlas.org/wiki/4_1>\nHyperbolic volume: 2.02988321281931 ± 1×10⁻¹⁴  (SnapPy / Bloch-Wigner)\nRef: [turaev2010] https://doi.org/10.1515/9783110221831 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.trefoilEntry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.trefoilEntry","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L94-L106","doc":"**Trefoil (3₁)** — the simplest non-trivial knot.\nQOU identity: **Electron** (Generation 1).  The trefoil's braid group\nB₃ monodromy generates the branching structure of Bring's Surface.\n\nKnot Atlas: <http://katlas.org/wiki/3_1>\nHyperbolic volume: 0  (torus knot — non-hyperbolic)\nJones polynomial: −t⁻⁴ + t⁻³ + t⁻¹ ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.unknotEntry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.unknotEntry","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L77-L92","doc":"**Unknot (0₁)** — the trivial knot.\nQOU identity: **Neutrino**.  Represents the SU(2) vacuum state and\nthe baseline vacuum drag with zero crossing number.\n\nKnot Atlas: <http://katlas.org/wiki/0_1>\nHyperbolic volume: 0  (non-hyperbolic) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.KnotEntry.atlas_url","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.KnotEntry.atlas_url","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L73-L73","doc":"Persistent URL to The Knot Atlas wiki page. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.KnotEntry.identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.KnotEntry.identity","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L71-L71","doc":"The QOU particle this knot represents. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.KnotEntry.volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.KnotEntry.volume","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Hyperbolic volume of the knot complement (SnapPy). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.KnotEntry.braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.KnotEntry.braid","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L67-L67","doc":"Braid word (Markov-closure encoding) from `QOU.KnotTheory`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.KnotEntry.ab_index","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.KnotEntry.ab_index","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L65-L65","doc":"Alexander-Briggs index, e.g. `\"4_1\"`. Primary key. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.KnotEntry.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.KnotEntry.mk","kind":"ctor","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.KnotEntry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.KnotEntry","kind":"structure","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L58-L73","doc":"A fully-specified knot registry entry.\n\nEach entry is the \"settled type\" for one knot in the QOU formalization:\nit pins the Alexander-Briggs name, braid word, computed volume,\nphysical identity, and external reference URL. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.instReprQOUIdentity.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.instReprQOUIdentity.repr","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.instReprQOUIdentity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.instReprQOUIdentity","kind":"instance","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.instDecidableEqQOUIdentity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.instDecidableEqQOUIdentity","kind":"instance","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.QOUIdentity.nucleon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.QOUIdentity.nucleon","kind":"ctor","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L52-L53","doc":"The nucleon — Borromean rings, color-exchange entanglement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.QOUIdentity.strongForce","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.QOUIdentity.strongForce","kind":"ctor","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L50-L51","doc":"The strong force — Hopf link, internal binding energy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.QOUIdentity.photon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.QOUIdentity.photon","kind":"ctor","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L48-L49","doc":"The photon — background flux on the exceptional divisor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.QOUIdentity.higgsField","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.QOUIdentity.higgsField","kind":"ctor","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L46-L47","doc":"The Higgs field / mass mechanism — figure-eight 4₁, amphichiral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.QOUIdentity.tauLepton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.QOUIdentity.tauLepton","kind":"ctor","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L44-L45","doc":"The tau lepton — Generation 3, septafoil T_{2,7} on Reeb divisor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.QOUIdentity.muon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.QOUIdentity.muon","kind":"ctor","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L42-L43","doc":"The muon — Generation 2, cinquefoil T_{2,5} on Reeb divisor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.QOUIdentity.electron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.QOUIdentity.electron","kind":"ctor","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L40-L41","doc":"The electron — Generation 1, B₃ monodromy source for Bring's Surface. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.QOUIdentity.neutrino","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.QOUIdentity.neutrino","kind":"ctor","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L38-L39","doc":"The neutrino — trivial knot, SU(2) vacuum baseline. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotRegistry.QOUIdentity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotRegistry.QOUIdentity","kind":"inductive","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotRegistry.lean#L36-L54","doc":"The physical particle a knot encodes in the QOU framework. ","signatureChunk":0}]}